From 6f6c0dcc9dd80ffc052b4d4fa7bd48d22551dedc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PowerVLC <powervlc@localhost>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bdj: expose the profile-5 graphics offset sequence control

Some Sony 3D menu Xlets require GraphicsOffsetSequenceControl while setting
up their coherent screen configuration. Returning null aborts the graphics
path after the correct menu background playlist has already started, leaving
an indefinitely looping background with no buttons.

Retain the selected sequence id and implement the listener contract. The
actual per-frame disparity continues to be delivered through the profile-5
graphics configuration and ARGB overlay offset path.
---
 .../GraphicsOffsetSequenceControlImpl.java    | 64 ++++++++++++++++++++
 .../media/content/playlist/Handler.java       |  3 +-
 2 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/GraphicsOffsetSequenceControlImpl.java

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/GraphicsOffsetSequenceControlImpl.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/GraphicsOffsetSequenceControlImpl.java
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/media/content/playlist/GraphicsOffsetSequenceControlImpl.java
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+/*
+ * This file is part of libbluray.
+ * Copyright (C) 2026 PowerVLC authors
